2.3 Sample preparation and measuring
To investigate the effects of L-PBF process parameters on surface roughness, iFusion150 (Intech Additive Solution, Karnataka, 560058, India) was employed. The machine is equipped with two ytterbium fiber lasers, each possessing a maximum power of 500 W and scanning speeds of up to 7000 mm/s. The process chamber underwent a careful purge with 99.99% argon to ensure an oxygen-free environment. Powder storage was maintained in a vacuum desiccator to eliminate moisture infiltration, while the base plate was preheated to 200 °C to establish a controlled environment for the stored powder. Cubic specimens, designed with precision at 15mm × 15mm × 15mm using SolidWorks® CAD software (2023 SP0.1 professional version), were modeled adhering to ISO 4288:1997 [49] standards as depicted in Fig. 4. Surface roughness measurements were conducted using a Mitutoyo Surftest SJ-301, with specified reference and evaluation lengths set at 2.5 mm and 12.5 mm, respectively, aligning precisely with guidelines [50]. Ahead of measuring the surface roughness, the surface was prepared to ensure it was free from any debris. The SJ-301 was
